- op: discuss  # 3ed3
  at: '2026-10-03T06:42:07Z'  # 3ed3
  by: agent  # 3ed3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3ed3
  clock: 5  # 3ed3
  nonce: 3ed3  # 3ed3
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). CURRENT, but Go is one case of a defect in all six def/use languages. Title updated.\n- cfg_nodes/go.yaml for_statement has only body_child (gap comment still there); cfg.py:1013's loop handler records only the condition, and only when condition_child is set. Its docstring claims the header holds the \"iterator for for\", which is false in every mapping.\n- Repro (CFG + def/use as ddg_build does it):\n  - Go `if err := do(a); err != nil`: only `err != nil` (err never defined, the do(a) call absent).\n  - Go `for j := 0; j < n; j++`: body only (condition and update missing too).\n  - Go `for _, e := range os.Environ()`: e never defined.\n  - Python `for v in os.environ:`: v never defined, os.environ never used.\n  - Rust `for v in std::env::args()`: v never defined.\n  - TS `for (const v of items)`: v never defined.\n  - C/TS/Java classic for: condition only (init and update missing).\n  - Java enhanced for: loop variable never defined.\n- The Python for-loop variable is probably the highest-volume case (unmeasured).\n- Still cited by taint.py guard comments (~4450, ~5026); the regression test is now test_taint.py:2376 (the discussion's 1842 drifted). ADR-0017 line 688 cites the Go gap; line 974 requires extractor tests to cover loop variables.\n- Side finding, filed today as WI-tozar: a python walrus / JS-TS nested assignment is recorded as a use, never a definition.\n- NOT CHECKED: the caddy approximate->precise case; corpus volume."  # 3ed3
- op: discuss  # 5e19
  at: '2026-10-03T21:39:37Z'  # 5e19
  by: agent  # 5e19
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5e19
  clock: 6  # 5e19
  nonce: '5e19'  # 5e19
  message: "Bears on INV-dukam (kanor run 2026-10-03): with exec.Command unrowed in a probe arm, the relocated finding at cmd.Run() could only be confirmed when the use of `cmd` is recorded; the idiomatic `if err := cmd.Run(); err != nil` records no use of cmd (this item), so on containers-storage unshareFn the flow fell from precise to approximate. Together with WI-jahip (a field store kills the receiver's reaching definition) these two gaps decide whether executor relocation can be precise in Go."  # 5e19
- op: discuss  # a520
  at: '2026-10-05T09:15:00Z'  # a520
  by: agent  # a520
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a520
  clock: 7  # a520
  nonce: a520  # a520
  message: "Fixed on branch jgstern-agent/fix/losod (worktree ~/hg_wt/losod, based on c1dd831558; commits 11a10f98b0, 445768867b, a9e3a869f4, 2c26be3459; not pushed). This is one statement-model fix in the shared CfgBuilder, done together with WI-faful. New cfg_nodes keys: initializer_child (conditional, loop, switch), and update_child, header_child and header_is_node (loop). Header parts become statements that define their bindings before the body. A for-each binding with no node of its own is recorded at the loop node, with CfgStatement.extent_end_byte cut at the body so the coverage gates do not count the body. Child references gain three forms: a/b, a|b and unfielded[:except=..]. Extractors: a go range_clause handler, a java enhanced-for header handler, and rust let_condition/let_chain handlers.\nBehavioral evidence: verify-claims with host_secret -> host_fs/network, base c1dd831558 vs branch. Go if-init sink: structural -> ddg/confirmed. Go if-init source: structural -> ddg/confirmed. Go range over os.Environ() (caddy shape): structural -> ddg/confirmed. Go for-clause: structural -> ddg/confirmed. Python for over os.environ.values(): not_attempted -> ddg/confirmed. Rust for over env::vars(): structural -> ddg/confirmed. TS for-of and classic for: structural -> ddg/confirmed. Java enhanced-for and classic for: not_attempted -> ddg/confirmed. C classic for with getenv: structural -> ddg/confirmed. Controls (Go and Python, source in the header, sink fed a constant) read ddg_mixed/escaped, not confirmed. Corpus, 6 repos, no verdict moved: containers-storage unshareFn's `if err := cmd.Run(); err != nil` now confirms os.Stdin -> Cmd.Run.\nsmart-test, BASE_BRANCH=c1dd831558, 422 affected test files: 12856 passed, with \"All changed source files are at 100% coverage\". Four unrelated failures were deselected: the rust extern-block test after the grammar upgrade, the auto-pr test that BASE_BRANCH leaks into, and two watcher-lifecycle timing tests. The hypothesis flake was also deselected. The caddy repo is not in the corpus, so the reference case was reproduced as a fixture only. Residual binding constructs are filed as WI-nohuv-tujuk-humal-numuh-posip-fonun-butir-kuroz. Full report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/losod.md"  # a520
